+{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"c996719e-8c90-4502-abf1-b5866849090b","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_jSwUPJSHDAYpG4Xj3lO80595","name":"Workflow","input":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'plugin-marketplace',\n  description: 'Build all 5 plugin marketplace modules + integration layer + tests',\n  phases: [\n    { title: 'Setup', detail: 'npm install' },\n    { title: 'Modules', detail: 'implement 5 modules in parallel' },\n    { title: 'Integrate', detail: 'compose createMarketplace' },\n    { title: 'Verify', detail: 'build, lint, test' },\n  ],\n}\n\nphase('Setup')\nawait agent('Run npm install in /workspace', { label: 'npm install', phase: 'Setup' })\nlog('Dependencies installed')\n\nphase('Modules')\n\n// 1. Registry module\nawait agent(`Create /workspace/src/registry/index.ts implementing RegistryService from src/types.ts.\n\nUse better-sqlite3 for persistence. The database file should be at a configurable path (passed via constructor).\n\nRequirements:\n- Table 'plugins' with columns: name TEXT, version TEXT, description TEXT, author TEXT, entry_point TEXT, permissions TEXT (JSON array), PRIMARY KEY(name, version)\n- register(manifest): insert a new plugin version. If a row with the same (name, version) already exists, throw an error.\n- get(name): return the latest version (highest semver) of a plugin. If none, return null.\n- getVersion(name, version): return specific version. Return null if not found.\n- list(): return all plugin versions (all manifests).\n- search(query): return all plugin manifests where name, description, or author contains the query (case-insensitive).\n- remove(name, version): delete a specific version. Return true if deleted, false if not found.\n- listVersions(name): return all version strings for a plugin.\n- update(name, version, updates): partially update a manifest. Updates can include description, author, entryPoint, permissions, dependencies. Throw if not found.\n\nExport a class PluginRegistry that implements RegistryService. Constructor takes dbPath?: string (default ':memory:').\nCreate the database and table in the constructor.\nUse prepared statements for performance.\nUse WAL mode for the database.\n\nImport types only from '../types.js' (note the .js extension for ESM).\nImport Database from 'better-sqlite3'.\nAlso import semver for version comparison (use semver.compare to sort for \"latest version\" in get()).\nUse try/catch with error messages.\nHandle JSON serialization for permissions and dependencies fields.\n\nDo NOT import from other module directories.`, { label: 'Registry module', phase: 'Modules' })\n\n// 2. Resolver module\nawait agent(`Create /workspace/src/resolver/index.ts implementing ResolverService from src/types.ts.\n\nUse the semver npm package. Do NOT use any persistence.\n\nRequirements:\n- satisfies(version, range): return semver.satisfies(version, range)\n- maxSatisfying(versions, range): return semver.maxSatisfying(versions, range)\n- validRange(range): return semver.validRange(range) !== null (just check if it's a valid range)\n- resolve(constraints, available): Given an array of VersionConstraint objects and a Record<string, string[]> mapping package names to available version arrays, return an array of ResolvedVersion objects. For each constraint, find the maxSatisfying version from the available list. If any constraint cannot be satisfied, throw an Error with message \"Cannot satisfy constraint: <name>@<range>\".\n\nImport semver and types from '../types.js'.\n\nExport a class VersionResolver implementing ResolverService.\n\nDo NOT import from other module directories.`, { label: 'Resolver module', phase: 'Modules' })\n\n// 3. Runner module\nawait agent(`Create /workspace/src/runner/index.ts implementing RunnerService from src/types.ts.\n\nUse Node.js 'vm' module for sandboxing. NOT vm2.\n\nRequirements:\n- execute(code, context?): Run code string in a VM sandbox.\n  - Create a new V8 context with vm.createContext() using a sandbox object.\n  - Pass context variables into the sandbox.\n  - Run the code with vm.runInContext().\n  - Wrap in a try/catch. On success, return { success: true, output: <return value>, duration: <ms as number>, memoryUsed: <process.memoryUsage().heapUsed - before>, error: undefined }.\n  - On error, return { success: false, output: undefined, duration: <ms as number>, memoryUsed: <ms as number>, error: <error.message> }.\n  - Measure start time with performance.now() / Date.now().\n  - Measure memory before/after with process.memoryUsage().heapUsed.\n\n- executeWithTimeout(code, timeoutMs, context?): Same as execute but with a timeout.\n  - Use an AbortController-like pattern or a Promise.race with setTimeout.\n  - The vm module doesn't natively support timeout well. Use vm.Script with options { timeout: timeoutMs } — vm.createContext + script.runInContext accepts a timeout option in milliseconds.\n  - If timeout is exceeded, vm.Script throws with an error containing 'timeout'. Catch it and return { success: false, output: undefined, duration: timeoutMs, memoryUsed: 0, error: 'Execution timed out' }.\n\nThe sandbox should expose a minimal global context: { console: { log: (...args) => capturedLogs.push(args) }, setTimeout: undefined, setInterval: undefined, require: undefined, process: undefined, Buffer: undefined }.\n\nActually, for capturing console.log output, collect it into an array and include it in the output. The returned output can be an object { returnValue: <last expression>, logs: [...] } for successful execution.\n\nImport vm from 'node:vm'.\nImport { SandboxResult } from '../types.js'.\n\nExport a class SandboxedRunner implementing RunnerService.\n\nDo NOT import from other module directories.`, { label: 'Runner module', phase: 'Modules' })\n\n// 4. Review System module\nawait agent(`Create /workspace/src/reviews/index.ts implementing ReviewService from src/types.ts.\n\nUse better-sqlite3 for persistence.\n\nRequirements:\n- Table 'reviews' with columns: id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, plugin_name TEXT, plugin_version TEXT, user_id TEXT, rating INTEGER, comment TEXT, flagged INTEGER DEFAULT 0, created_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now'))\n- addReview(review): Insert a review with pluginName, pluginVersion, userId, rating, comment. Return the full Review object (including the auto-generated id, createdAt, and flagged=false).\n- getReviews(pluginName): Return all non-flagged reviews for a plugin (ordered by created_at DESC).\n- getAverageRating(pluginName): Return the average rating for a plugin, EXCLUDING flagged reviews. Return 0 if no non-flagged reviews exist. The rating should be a number (not null).\n- flagReview(reviewId): Set flagged=1 for the given review ID. If not found, throw an error.\n- getFlaggedReviews(): Return all reviews where flagged=1.\n- removeReview(reviewId): Delete a review by ID. Return true if deleted, false if not found.\n- getReviewsByUser(userId): Return all reviews by a user (regardless of flagged status).\n- getReviewCount(pluginName): Return the count of non-flagged reviews for a plugin.\n\nExport a class ReviewSystem implementing ReviewService. Constructor takes dbPath?: string (default ':memory:').\nCreate the table in constructor.\nUse WAL mode.\n\nImport types from '../types.js'.\nImport Database from 'better-sqlite3'.\n\nDo NOT import from other module directories.`, { label: 'Review System module', phase: 'Modules' })\n\n// 5. Dependency Graph module\nawait agent(`Create /workspace/src/deps/index.ts implementing DepsService from src/types.ts.\n\nThis module analyzes plugin dependency relationships using the RegistryService.\n\nRequirements:\n- buildTree(name, registry): Build a DependencyNode tree for a plugin.\n  - Look up the plugin via registry.get(name) to get the latest version.\n  - For each dependency in the plugin's dependencies field, recursively build subtrees.\n  - Return a DependencyNode with nam